460
00:39:24,721 --> 00:39:31,120
No other photosynthetic organism is able to compete and survive in those conditions.

461
00:39:31,121 --> 00:39:36,880
Thermoacidophiles like cyanidium survive in these extreme conditions by generating

462
00:39:36,881 --> 00:39:43,880
special enzymes that protect their cells from decaying in the superheated acidic water.

463
00:39:44,980 --> 00:39:49,060
The discovery of these unique enzymes has ensured that thermoacidophiles won't be written

464
00:39:49,061 --> 00:39:51,740
off as simply scientific curiosities.

465
00:39:51,741 --> 00:39:58,740
If a microorganism can live at a very high temperature or a very low pH, then it's not

466
00:39:59,200 --> 00:40:04,320
a large leap to believe that it's making enzymes that can also survive under those conditions.

467
00:40:04,321 --> 00:40:10,800
And those same enzymes may have application in industrial processes.

468
00:40:10,801 --> 00:40:16,980
Yellowstone is only one of several thermoacidophile hotspots.

469
00:40:16,981 --> 00:40:22,040
So called bioprospectors search for specialized thermoacidophile enzymes in some of the most

470
00:40:22,041 --> 00:40:25,080
remote places on Earth.

471
00:40:25,081 --> 00:40:30,320
Among the places we've looked for new enzymes is in the microorganisms that live at the

472
00:40:30,321 --> 00:40:32,900
bottom of the deep ocean.

473
00:40:32,901 --> 00:40:37,580
In that location you have hot sulfurous gases, hydrogen sulfide,

474
00:40:37,581 --> 00:40:43,280
bouching through fissures in the Earth's crust, generating temperatures up to 250 Fahrenheit.

475
00:40:43,281 --> 00:40:49,920
Living in near boiling acid, hyperthermophiles produce an enzyme

476
00:40:49,921 --> 00:40:54,040
that's being synthesized to produce clean burning ethanol fuel from corn.

477
00:40:54,041 --> 00:40:59,320
It works on the starch molecule to break it down into smaller fragments,

478
00:40:59,321 --> 00:41:02,920
the conditions under which the starch liquefaction is carried out are

479
00:41:02,921 --> 00:41:06,320
characteristically high temperature and low pH.

480
00:41:06,321 --> 00:41:13,320
While thermoacidophile enzymes may one day help pioneer a biological industrial revolution,

481
00:41:13,321 --> 00:41:19,320
their existence also raises questions about other extreme environments where life may exist,

482
00:41:19,321 --> 00:41:24,320
both here on Earth and throughout the solar system.

483
00:41:24,321 --> 00:41:33,560
From the steaming pools of Yellowstone to the industrial processes that mold our world,

484
00:41:33,561 --> 00:41:37,640
acid is perhaps the most ubiquitous chemical on the planet.

485
00:41:37,641 --> 00:41:41,920
By taming its dangers, mankind harnesses its gifts.

486
00:41:41,921 --> 00:41:45,000
Not bad for a substance that leaves a sour taste in your mouth.

